course: dictionary
lesson: 9522
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and a dictionary lists each one. To choose the right meaning, read the words around the word. These are its context, and they give clues. Stilt is a good example, because it has three meanings in the dictionary.
explain: «Stilt roots hold mangroves up in soft mud.» The words mangroves and mud tell you that a stilt here is a root, a kind of support that holds a plant up. A root is not a pole for walking, so the walking meaning does not fit. Always ask: which meaning would make sense in this sentence?
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one. If it sounds silly, try another meaning from the dictionary. Words can also be used in phrases, like «on stilts», which is a useful clue too.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists them as 1), 2), 3) and so on.
fact: A stilt is a pair of long poles with footrests that you stand on to walk high above the ground.
fact: A stilt can also be a tall post that holds a house or building up above water or the ground.
fact: A stilt is also a wading bird with very long thin pink legs.
fact: Context clues, like «stilt roots» or a stilt walker at a fair, show you which meaning the writer means.
exercise: «The stilt walker at the fair towered over the crowd.» What is a stilt walker? | A bird that wades in shallow water | A person who builds houses on posts | A clown who juggles balls | *A performer who walks on tall poles with footrests
exercise: «Stilt roots hold mangroves up in soft mud.» Which meaning of stilt fits here? | Tall poles with footrests for walking | A wading bird with long pink legs | A pair of shoes for running | *Tall supports that hold a plant up above the ground
exercise: «The village had houses built on stilts above the flood water.» What does on stilts mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Hidden under the water | *Held up on tall posts above the water | Standing on poles for a race
test: «A stilt stood alone in the shallow pond, its long thin pink legs never moving.» What is the stilt in this sentence? | A pole for walking | A post holding up a house | A stick for a game | *A wading bird
test: «Scientists put tiny stilts on desert ants.» Which meaning of stilt fits this sentence best? | A wading bird with long pink legs | A root that holds up a plant | *Tiny poles with footrests for the ants to walk on | A post that holds up a house
exam: «The stilt walker crossed the street, then the stilt roots of the mangrove and the stilt house by the river all came into view.» Which meaning of stilt is used for the house? | A bird that wades in water | A root that takes in air | Long poles that a person walks on | *A tall post that holds a building up above the ground
